   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>0.00456</p>\n<p>Case 2: The absolute value of the number is less than 1.</p>\n<p>Step 1: Count the number of digits between the decimal and the first non-zero digit. Label this <i>n</i>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"n = 2\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: Starting with the first non-zero digit of the number, write the digits. If the number was negative, include the negative sign.</p>\n<p>456</p>\n<p>Step 3: If there is more than one digit, place the decimal after the first digit from Step 2.</p>\n<p>4.56</p>\n<p>Step 4: Multiply the number from 3 by <span data-math=\"{10^{ - \\left( {n + 1} \\right)}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"4.56 \\times {10^{ - 3}}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"4.56 \\times {10^{ - 3}}\">4.56 \\times {10^{ - 3}}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
